  <p class="gd-byline" style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:12.5px;letter-spacing:.05em;color:var(--blue-soft);opacity:.9;margin:16px 0 0">By <a href="/about" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px">Heliski Travel Team</a> · Updated 9 Aug 2026</p>
  <p class="gd-lede">Heli-skiing is sometimes pictured as a male-heavy world of big spines and bravado. The reality is different and far more welcoming: it is about skiing ability and good judgement, not gender, and women ski Iceland's Troll Peninsula superbly every season. This is an honest guide to heli-skiing for women, the ability you truly need, what a trip looks like, how to prepare and how to make it your own, before you look at <a href="/packages">the packages</a>.</p>
